// CF-2: `>=` alone keeps fp32 where every other comparison demotes to
// fx12.
//
// Measured, three ways (literal right-hand side, varying right-hand side,
// reversed operands): a lone `<`, `>`, `<=`, `==` or `!=` feeding a kill
// is emitted at fx12 precision, and a lone `>=` is not.  It is a property
// of the opcode, not of the operands.  Nobody in this room has a
// mechanism for it, so it is pinned here rather than explained: a later
// tidy-up that "normalises" the precision table would otherwise walk the
// container away from the reference with every test still green.
//
// Writing the same predicate as `0.5 <= c.a` DOES get the fx12 form,
// because the reference keeps the source operator - see the twin fixture
// fp_discard_ge_rev_f.  The two must NOT compile to the same instruction.
void main(float4 c : TEXCOORD0, out float4 o : COLOR)
{
    if (c.a >= 0.5) discard;
    o = c;
}
